+# Next operator phase: review and development completion
+
+Status: not ready for production execution. All 21 preparation slots stay null;
+the Request029 compiler and controller continue refusing production.
+
+Owner: home.servers operator, with Forge reviewing the closed evidence contract.
+Current candidate scope is the Request032 synthetic VM108 root only. Existing
+production scheduler and all production identities remain unchanged.
+
+Remaining code/integration gaps:
+
+1. Map the copied scheduler and manual adapter to reviewed production helper
+   contracts, including their side effects and recovery semantics. Current helpers
+   deliberately implement synthetic behavior. No production adapter is installed.
+2. Compare a metadata-only production catalog census against the explicitly
+   supported profile. Add reviewed handling or explicit rejection for every
+   unsupported production object; synthetic equality cannot answer that question.
+3. Bind persistent boot/admission units to a reviewed production service graph,
+   control-directory ownership and container identities. Templates and transient
+   ordering tests are implemented, but installation and a real reboot are unproved.
+4. Define the production filesystem/signing capture policy, private off-host
+   destination and restore acceptance contract. Arbitrary Mac metadata is not
+   supported by the synthetic fixture adaptation. No private production bytes
+   have been copied into this development workspace or relay.
+
+Next authorized development work should close those concrete mappings, repeat
+failure tests on final bytes, and review the production metadata census. A later
+immutable production proposal must bind owner, exact source and service IDs,
+current holds, machine/boot policy, private destination, credentials by reference,
+maintenance and serving-restoration deadlines, and an explicit rollback to the
+unchanged incumbent. Those production values are intentionally not fabricated.
+
+If any admission, source, hold, boot, catalog or finalizer proof fails, retain
+pending intent and stop new effects. Restore only the bound incumbent and original
+writer controls under the target recovery owner. Do not clear intent based on
+elapsed time. After synthetic acceptance, stop only recorded Request032 container
+IDs and transient startup units; retain their state, journals and source versions.
+Production execution, renewal, rotation, transfer, cutover and resume require a
+separate explicit authorization. Expiry does not expand this request.
